00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:50.620
And I have the good fortune
of having some of my customers

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:54.520
sitting along with me, will
join me shortly on this panel.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:01:00.180
So without further ado,
being in the business

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:01.540
for such a long time--

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:05.220
and I've worked as both an
employee of a large corporation

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:07.800
and a management consultant.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:10.890
And now I'm working as--

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:14.850
helping companies come up and
drive breakthrough innovation

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:17.380
using the latest technologies.

00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:19.170
The key thing that
has stood out for me

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:22.680
is that typically,
a lot of enterprises

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:25.860
end up in having
focus on what I call

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:29.070
as a front end of the
enterprise value chain.

00:01:29.070 --> 00:01:32.550
I define that more as
marketing the front end

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:35.310
of the whole business,
the customer-facing side

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:39.000
of a business in the value
chain, marketing sales.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.370
And then you have the
operations and the supply chain,

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:44.480
which for our reference,
I'll define as the back end.

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:46.980
Typically, there's
been a lot of focus

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:50.550
on, how do you make the
profitability of the enterprise

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:53.820
or the customer experience
that an enterprise can

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:55.890
provide its customer seamless?

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:58.380
And we've seen
time and time again

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:02.700
that this has pretty much been
a challenge, even though there

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:05.160
have been advances
in technology.

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:08.220
Just to illustrate
that, I thought

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:11.460
this was a very apt
quote from Mark Anderson.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:15.570
Pretty much, he captured
this very well saying

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:19.620
that, well, there were a lot
of technical breakthrough

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:22.590
technology possibilities.

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:24.930
Really the business--
there was a challenge

00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:27.570
in how business could
achieve the results

00:02:27.570 --> 00:02:30.390
despite those
technological innovations.

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:33.210
And that it was
not only the fact

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:35.700
that it was the business
who was willing to drive,

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:39.330
but develop technology
challenges that still stop

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:43.060
the business from
attaining those goals.

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:48.850
So, that falls very perfectly
with my opening statement,

00:02:48.850 --> 00:02:52.230
which is essentially
the key to all this.

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:54.300
Driving the business
benefit starts

00:02:54.300 --> 00:03:00.520
by making sure that you are
able to take the process--

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:03.490
the process there is
basically people, process,

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:05.030
and technology--

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:10.350
and have it work seamlessly
from the front to back.

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:13.200
It starts with the customer
and ends with the customer.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:15.960
But for you guys as
enterprises, there's always

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:18.120
the front end or the
demand generation,

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:21.360
the marketing side
of the processes,

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:23.820
and then you have your
fulfillment processes,

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:28.390
which are mostly operational
that deals with supply chain.

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:33.780
So, the key thing is AI and
ML proposes some possibilities

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:37.770
to have a responsive back
end that can go hand-in-hand

00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:39.240
with the front end.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:44.940
And today's teams as you will
see in the panel discussion

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:47.880
is to give you some
ideas on how we

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:50.574
can see that
happening or, in fact,

00:03:50.574 --> 00:03:51.990
what are the
challenges that still

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:56.160
exist that need to be
overcome in order to make

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:57.840
it even better?

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:03.470
And how does AI and ML fall into
the strategic aspect as well as

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:07.190
a tactical aspect
of enabling this?

00:04:07.190 --> 00:04:09.560
So, a lot of
companies have already

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:16.310
started using AI on the
marketing side, to some extent,

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:18.050
even on the customer
relationship

00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:20.259
management and sales.

00:04:20.259 --> 00:04:24.680
AI has been seen to have given
very good results in this area.

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:28.850
The key is whether we can
follow that up and leverage

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:32.840
AI and ML also on the
operations and supply chain.

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:36.630
And that piece is
still evolving.

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:40.470
So just to encapsulate
this, pretty much

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:43.860
some of the key things
here are, you can come up

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:47.580
with a very good, efficient,
and targeted marketing leading

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:51.720
to competitive
advantage that can

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:53.700
be achieved through AI and ML.

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:56.550
It has been achieved through
traditional analytics

00:04:56.550 --> 00:04:57.330
to some extent.

00:04:57.330 --> 00:05:00.210
And you'll see, my
panelists talk about it.

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:04.290
And then the key here is
on the operations side

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:07.500
is doing exception
base demand planning.

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:10.710
Time and time again, when I
have provided solutions to large

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:13.020
customers or even
small customers,

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:15.180
even though they have
been good solutions--

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:20.580
and some of you are aware
of them like SAP, Oracle,

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:25.040
Value Gen Planning, SIPs,
advance supply chain planning--

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:28.260
every time we've implement it,
the customer has still come

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:31.130
back and asked, why can't I
do exception-based planning,

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:35.000
meaning, I need to only
know where the demand--

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:36.990
where do I have to pay
attention to my demand,

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:41.200
and where do I have to pay
attention to my supply?

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:45.915
So these are typical outcomes
where people have started

00:05:45.915 --> 00:05:48.570
using AI and ML we have seen.

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:49.890
And again we'll go--

00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:53.730
as the panelists talk about
it, hopefully this comes out.

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:57.000
It really helps, for example,
in coming up with the 360

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.580
view of the customer.

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:02.430
And that leads to increasing,
for example, your marketing

00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:08.130
campaign efficiencies, and helps
drive revenue on the front end.

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:11.850
On the back end, it really
helps if you do this right

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:15.700
by coming up with a good
customer experience,

00:06:15.700 --> 00:06:18.150
especially in
retail, where retail

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:19.980
has to be very
responsive, especially

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:22.560
with omni channel, et cetera.

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:26.490
And it allows you to do this
while maintaining productivity

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:28.610
and profitability.

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:32.190
And to really come
to this piece where

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:34.080
you can have the
true benefits, you

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:36.810
have to see some sort
of implementation

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:38.010
across the enterprise.

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:40.290
That's the goal.

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:44.880
So, how can ML drive
your transformation

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:45.760
of your business?

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:50.460
These are the three key elements
in that whole value chain.

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:54.570
And then, there's the marketing
ML, there's a demand ML,

00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:55.650
and there's a supply ML.

00:06:55.650 --> 00:06:56.760
I'm just simplifying this.

00:06:56.760 --> 00:07:00.810
You heard it yesterday and
today, a lot of AI and ML

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:02.700
are making things simpler.

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:05.940
So to keep it simple
and easy, those

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:10.290
are the branding that
we have come up with.

00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:13.700
And we'll expand into
this in the panel.

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:16.510
So without further
ado, I would like

00:07:16.510 --> 00:07:19.870
to invite my panelists
up here to join me.

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:23.750
And we have a great set
off panelists today.

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:26.980
They are our customers.

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:32.230
And we will talk with them
on each of their experiences

00:07:32.230 --> 00:07:36.320
that deal with the front end
and the back end of the process.

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:38.110
What are their thoughts?

00:07:38.110 --> 00:07:42.310
What do they see as strategic
elements, the tactical elements

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:46.060
and their experiences in
trying to leverage AI and ML

00:07:46.060 --> 00:07:47.650
in accomplishing
what I just said?

